# Tooling: uv

This project uses [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/) for virtualenvs, locking, and running commands.

## Commands

- `uv sync` — create/update `.venv` from `uv.lock` (includes dev dependency group)
- `uv sync --extra pdf` — add optional PDF support
- `uv sync --extra vllm` — GPU inference server for NuExtract3 (large; CUDA required)
- `uv sync --all-extras` — all optional feature extras (pdf, train, transformers, vllm)
- `uv lock` — refresh lockfile after `pyproject.toml` changes
- `uv run pytest` / `uv run docpii` / `uv run ruff check src tests scripts` — run in project env

Do **not** use bare `pip install` or manual `python -m venv` for project setup unless the user
explicitly requests it.

After changing dependencies, run `uv lock` then `uv sync`.
